# ASan/LSan REGRESSION FIXTURE — `f(&(*box).field)` used to CLONE THE WHOLE
# STRUCT to take an address of, and leak the clone.
#
# THE LEAK. Before the Family-1 chokepoint, an `&`-argument projecting through a
# Box deref fell past the bare-`&*b` fast-path into the value-copy read path.
# That read emitted `Holder__clone(...)` — a whole-struct clone, whose
# resource fields are deep-copied by `gorget_string_clone_to_owned` — took the
# address of a field INSIDE that clone, and handed it to the callee. The callee's
# write landed on the clone, the clone was never dropped, and the caller's value
# was untouched: a silent wrong answer AND an unbounded leak in one shape.
#
# AXIS + CELL (Core #12): the MEMORY-VALIDITY axis at the
# `&(*box).<resource field>` cell. ⚠ It is specifically a bare `String` field
# that leaks — the `Vector`/`Dict`/resource-struct field cells emit the same
# `Holder__clone` but their clone temps happen to be drop-registered, so they
# lose the write WITHOUT leaking. Sampling only those cells is a false negative;
# that is why this fixture pins the String one.
#
# ggdef is STRUCTURALLY BLIND to this class — it adjudicates value semantics and
# cannot observe an unfreed allocation — so ASan on the real backends is the only
# instrument that can see it (Core #13).
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the pre-fix compiler under `detect_leaks=1`:
#     ERROR: LeakSanitizer: detected memory leaks
#     Direct leak of 5 byte(s) in 1 object(s)
#       gorget_string_clone_to_owned <- Holder__clone <- main
#     SUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: 5 byte(s) leaked in 1 allocation(s).   exit 99
# Post-fix: exit 0, no report.
#
# ⚠ SHAPE NOTE — why the String field is seeded with a LITERAL and assigned a
# COMPUTED string, rather than the reverse. The leaked allocation is made by
# `clone_to_owned` on the FIELD, so it fires from a literal seed just as well
# (RED-verified above — not a false negative). Seeding with a literal keeps the
# POST-fix state clean: assigning over a static-literal slot has no old heap
# pointee to release, which sidesteps the separately-filed
# "re-assigning through a `&`-param never drops the param slot's OLD pointee"
# leak (TODO.md, `Vector[int]` cell filed; the `String` cell appended by this
# round). Seeding with a heap string instead makes this fixture RED post-fix for
# THAT unrelated defect and it would guard nothing. The ASSIGNED value is still
# heap-forced (`mk()` concatenates), so the write itself is a real allocation.
#
# GUARDED MECHANISM: `try_resolve_place`'s `Expr::Deref` arm plus the `Deref`
# object arm of `try_resolve_field_place`, which resolve the field to a place
# INSIDE the box instead of cloning the struct to address a copy. Short-circuit
# the producer to `None` and the `Holder__clone` leak returns.
struct Holder:
    String s
    int n

String mk():
    return "gg" + "-payload"

int seed():
    return 1

void set_str(String &x):
    x = mk()

void bump(int &k):
    k = k + 1

void main():
    Box[Holder] b = Box(Holder("base", seed()))

    set_str(&(*b).s)
    print((*b).s)

    int i = 0
    while i < 8:
        bump(&(*b).n)
        i = i + 1
    print((*b).n)
